1459-	   Restricts the set of socket address families accessible to the processes of this unit. Takes "none", or a
1460-	   space-separated list of address family names to allow-list, such as AF_UNIX, AF_INET or AF_INET6. When
1461-	   "none" is specified, then all address families will be denied. When prefixed with "~" the listed address
1462-	   families will be applied as deny list, otherwise as allow list. Note that this restricts access to the
1463-	   socket(2) system call only. Sockets passed into the process by other means (for example, by using socket
1464-	   activation with socket units, see systemd.socket(5)) are unaffected. Also, sockets created with
1465-	   socketpair() (which creates connected AF_UNIX sockets only) are unaffected. Note that this option has no
1466-	   effect on 32-bit x86, s390, s390x, mips, mips-le, ppc, ppc-le, ppc64, ppc64-le and is ignored (but works
1467-	   correctly on other ABIs, including x86-64). Note that on systems supporting multiple ABIs (such as
